  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1052 PM CDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nThe bulk of the heavy precipitation is expected to end by Wednesday \nmorning as a dry slot punches eastward on the southern end of the \nupper low. Although some lingering scattered showers are a good bet \nthrough much of Wednesday, additional rainfall totals will only be \nlight. Another window for severe storms will then open Wednesday \nafternoon and evening, this time across the Rolling Plains along and \neast of a dryline. This threat should concentrate mainly to our \neast, but a few instances of large hail and damaging winds could \nmaterialize on Wednesday over our eastern zones. For the rest of the \nweek, the forecast generally trends drier and cooler. There will be \nsome potential for a few showers late week mainly off the Caprock, \nbut our current expectation is for most locations to remain dry \nThursday and beyond. The more noticable change will be much cooler \ntemperatures with highs currently forecast in the 60s and 70s \nThursday and Friday.",
